# Test: the non-identifier-VALUE reject, HYPHENATED-name half.
#
# Sibling of `directive_value_int_error.gg` (`directive trace=1`). Same parser
# arm, different route into it: `hot-reload` is assembled by the `-` continuation
# loop before the `=` is seen, so a regression that mangles hyphen handling can
# leave one of the two rows green while the other goes red. Both are pinned
# because neither covers the other.
#
# Rust gg: parse error, `expected identifier, found integer 1`. Self-host: the
# same verdict from `parse_directive_item`'s value check.
#
# Pinned on BOTH lanes: `directive_hot_reload_value_int_error` (Rust gg) and
# `sh_rejects_directive_hot_reload_value_int` (self-host driver).

directive hot-reload=1

void main():
    print("REACHED — the directive value was NOT validated on this lane")
